#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md:6
msgid "Sealed Traits"
msgstr ""

#: src/idiomatic/polymorphism/generics/sealed-traits.md:8
msgid ""
"Traits are normally extensible, meaning that downstream users can implement "
"our traits for their own types, and then our generic code can handle those "
"downstream types. Usually this is what we want, but sometimes we want to "
"define a trait where we control all of the implementations. To do this, we "
"can create a **sealed trait**."
msgstr ""

